/** \page asyncrecompute Async recompute

\section asyncrecompute_api Public contract

Document::recomputeAsync() returns a RecomputeHandle. The handle exposes a
document-owned identifier plus status, progress, completion, cancellation, and
bounded waiting.

Document::recompute() and Document::recomputeFeature() remain synchronous
in-process compatibility APIs. They execute on the document owner thread,
participate in an already-open native transaction, and do not silently create a
second transaction. Full-document recompute (and recursive feature recompute,
which delegates to it) preserves the established PendingRecompute, Recompute2,
two-pass, and observer ordering contracts. Non-recursive recomputeFeature()
preserves its established immediate single-feature behavior. Coordinator-owned
derived recompute remains isolated and folds validated results into its existing
outer transaction rather than executing arbitrary feature code live.

\section asyncrecompute_isolation Isolation and commit authority

The document-owned recompute coordinator captures immutable input and runs
eligible work detached from the live model in an isolated FreeCADCmd process.
Workers consume and produce bounded archives and never receive a live Document
or DocumentObject. Only DocumentCollaborationService and
DocumentCommitCoordinator may validate and commit results to the live document.

The explicitly asynchronous API has no caller-selected live or main-thread
execution fallback. Unsupported or unsafe objects produce a structured failure
and remain touched so the caller can inspect or resolve the error. The one
trusted application exception is the exact type-gated Spreadsheet transient
schema application step, which re-executes that built-in type under the commit
guard after isolated validation. This isolation guarantee does not describe the
synchronous compatibility APIs above.

\section asyncrecompute_python FeaturePython

App::FeaturePython is unsupported unless it explicitly opts in through
supportsAsyncRecompute(). An opted-in proxy must be fully serializable and its
execute path must not access FreeCADGui, Qt widgets, view providers, or other
GUI-thread state.

\section asyncrecompute_gui GUI and save behavior

GUI code that explicitly chooses recomputeAsync() must retain RecomputeHandle
instances and poll done() or status() with bounded event-loop slices, for example
from a short QTimer callback. It must not block the GUI thread waiting for an
asynchronous handle. The established Refresh command instead invokes the fast
synchronous owner-thread compatibility kernel; TransactionOnRecompute only
controls its undo grouping.

A canonical save attempted while recompute is active, or when a stale/failed
result leaves executable dirty work, returns RECOMPUTE_PENDING. A stale handle
still reports Stale even when a newer successful synchronous recompute already
settled the live feature; in that superseded case the clean document may be
saved. Callers should inspect the handle and retry unresolved work before save.

*/
